{"title": "Support always holds?", "type": "Myth or fact", "hooks": ["Three beliefs about support. None of them is true.", "Support always holds. Myth or fact?", "Most beginners believe all three of these about support."], "scenes": [{"kind": "hook", "vo": "Three beliefs about support. None of them is true.", "text": "Myth or fact?", "chart": null}, {"kind": "big", "text": "Volume into a level means nothing", "vo": "Belief one: volume rising into a level tells you nothing. Myth. When volume grows into the level, a break is likelier.", "chart": null}, {"kind": "big", "text": "You can skip the stop", "vo": "Belief two: a strong level means no stop. Myth. Levels hold often enough to trade, and break often enough that every trade needs one.", "chart": null}, {"kind": "chart", "chart": 0, "head": "Support always holds?", "show": 90, "vo": "Belief three, the big one: support always holds. Here, Snackwell Foods came back to its support on the one-minute chart.", "cues": [{"say": "came back to its support", "do": "mark", "i": 81, "label": "S", "side": "low", "tone": "teal"}], "win": [20, 115]}, {"kind": "chart", "chart": 0, "head": "Myth. It broke.", "vo": "Myth. It closed through the level and stayed through it. Twenty-five candles later, it was one percent lower.", "cues": [{"say": "stayed through it", "do": "reveal", "to": 115}, {"say": "one percent lower", "do": "shade", "from": 90, "to": 115, "tone": "red"}], "win": [20, 115], "show": 90}, {"kind": "big", "text": "A level is a clue", "vo": "So a level is a clue, never a promise. Count the touches, check the trend, watch the volume.", "chart": null}, {"kind": "outro", "text": "Practise on real charts", "vo": "Save this for your next level, and practise reading them at memestreet.net.", "chart": null}], "caption": "Support always holds. Myth or fact?\nThree beliefs about support levels, checked one by one.\nVolume into a level is a clue.\nEvery trade at a level needs a stop.\nAnd on this Snackwell Foods chart, support br